23.6 Wavelength and depth measured underground (1 kHz, lambda = 1000 m, delta = 159.2 m)
==============================================================================
  alpha = 1/delta = 0.00628141 Np/m, beta = 2pi/lambda = 0.00628319 rad/m, alpha/beta = 0.99972 -> tau = 44.992 deg, p = tan 2tau = 3533
  exact pi/500 = 0.00628319; 2pi/1000 = 0.00628319
  (c) sigma = 2 alpha beta/(w mu0) = 0.0099972 S/m; from delta alone 1/(pi f mu0 delta^2) = 0.0099943; from lambda alone beta^2/(pi f mu0) = 0.01
      clean: alpha = beta = pi/500: sigma = 2(pi/500)^2/(2pi 1e3 4pi 1e-7) = 0.01
  (b) vp = lambda f = 1e+06 m/s = c/299.8; lossless er = 10 would give c/sqrt(10) = 9.480e+07
  (d) eta = (1+j)/(sigma delta) = (1+j) pi/5 = 0.62832+0.62832j Ohm, |eta| = 0.88858 Ohm = sqrt(w mu0/sigma) = 0.88858; tau = 45 deg
  (e) eps from (beta^2 - alpha^2)/(w^2 mu): with alpha = beta exactly -> 0 (undetermined); with delta = 159.2: 50.87 eps0 (pure rounding noise)
      delta = 159.1500 m with lambda = 1000 m: er = (beta^2 - alpha^2)/(w^2 mu0 eps0) = -5.583
      delta = 159.1549 m with lambda = 1000 m: er = (beta^2 - alpha^2)/(w^2 mu0 eps0) = +3.085e-11
      delta = 159.2000 m with lambda = 1000 m: er = (beta^2 - alpha^2)/(w^2 mu0 eps0) = +50.87
      delta = 159.2500 m with lambda = 1000 m: er = (beta^2 - alpha^2)/(w^2 mu0 eps0) = +107.3
      relative change of delta from 159.15 to 159.25 m: 0.06%; er swing 112.9
      p > 10 needs eps < sigma/(10 w) = 1.592e-07 F/m -> er < 18000 (course eps0), 17975 (exact)
      dielectric-style er = (c/vp)^2 = 9e+04 (nonsense here)
      eta from sqrt(w mu0/sigma) with sigma = 1e-2: 0.88858 e^(j45) = 0.62832(1+j); from (1+j)/(sigma delta) with delta = 159.2: 0.62814(1+j)
      er =     1: p = 1.798e+05, delta = 159.16 m, lambda = 1000 m, |eta| = 0.88858 Ohm
      er =    10: p = 1.798e+04, delta = 159.16 m, lambda = 999.97 m, |eta| = 0.88858 Ohm
      er =  1000: p = 179.8, delta = 159.6 m, lambda = 997.22 m, |eta| = 0.88857 Ohm
  handbook wet earth er = 10: p = 18e9*1e-2/(1e3*10) = 1.8e+04

